==== SMOKE TEST INTERPRETATION ====
- HTTP server bound successfully on port 3000 ("Listening on http://localhost:3000").
- Process subsequently crashed on the first scheduled GET /app/installations
  call because APP_ID=1 is bogus and GitHub returned 404 "Integration not
  found", producing an unhandled promise rejection.
- This matches the case SESSION-1.md anticipated: "As long as the process
  starts and the HTTP server binds, that's enough for this stage; [auth]
  validation will succeed in the real deployment with the real KeyVault
  secret."
- /probot HTTP probe returned 000 because the process exited before curl
  could connect — NOT because the HTTP server failed to bind.
- Container starts cleanly: yes (image is good).
